{"title":"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three circles are mutually externally tangent. Two of the circles have radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If the area of the triangle formed by connecting their centers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/4131457f67c5dbfd8b1c6be1f74a47595a9bd3be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />, then the area of the third circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da40faccb9c89ca9cfed0f44129b44b014b42639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\pi$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the radius of the third circle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. The side lengths of the triangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c1dc5381adeb65db3161d2bb06a8816e2065c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b29fb713343686526286e79de5408485eb7408.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />. From Heron's Formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88f6314dede2744b0a51992fbc20b31748c3a524.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84=\\sqrt{(10+r)(r)(7)(3)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"193\" height=\"32\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3de67fa24f9f0814f5370b018e6370187cc6695c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84*84=r(10+r)*21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/014ba3f6aefe15106ced097aa019a469d1e593e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84*4=r(10+r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/a/75ab4358e03549b6feaabb3a45d18ef8ad978b8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84*4=14*24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"122\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/7/287da2b84ecc4e7e5d79209c2983c9bf7fd6251d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />. Thus the area of the circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/091e95b545b015289e2a4e337bd84d9cd9dd51b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{196}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"49\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005\">Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t={{{source}}}\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.ph